# The adaptive conformance scene, depth half
# (docs/adaptive-layout-plan.md §2): the arrangement axis is a PROPERTY
# on one node with two constructor spellings. A HANDLER flips row#0
# vertical and back — D2's user-driven toggle, the breakpoint
# mechanism's effect without its trigger (the breakpoint record is the
# milestone's next increment and drives this same prop).
#
# THE SUBJECT STAYS `row#0` THROUGH BOTH STATES: identity is the
# creation kind, presentation is the prop — which is what keeps every
# other scene's addressing stable while an app adapts.
#
# expect_axis reads the axis the RENDER used (a geometry-adjacent
# record on the container's own box reader; GTK answers its orientable
# back), never the model's field — a backend that ignored the write
# must fail, the expect_aligned rule one prop over.
expect label#0 "alpha"
expect_axis row#0 "horizontal"
expect_axis column@steady "vertical"
click button#0
expect_axis row#0 "vertical"
# And BACK — the revert half a one-way flip would leave unproven.
click button#0
expect_axis row#0 "horizontal"
